57bm-i16"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i16"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i16","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.125 (Spacing of compatible reverse-carry words)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.125, p. 79, label record:257bm-i16","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Consider two integer carry recurrences $b_i(m)+2u_i(m)=a_i(m)+u_i(m+1)$, $i=1,2$. If $a_1(k)=a_2(k)$ and the output bits at $k$ are $1$ and $0$, then the carry difference at $k+1$ is odd. If the coefficients and bits agree for the following $L$ positions, the difference at $k+L+1$ is $2^L$ times that odd integer. Consequently absolute terminal bounds $B_1,B_2$ give $2^L\\le B_1+B_2$. Lemma 6.46 states the exact identity and proves it by subtraction. The linked formal statements encode these agreements; they do not supply terminal bounds for an unrelated digit system.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-i16","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-i16","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i16%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfTrappingReturnCarry.overlappingMidpointReturns_twoPow_le_realBound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i16%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfTrappingReturnCarry.overlappingMidpointReturns_twoPow_le_realBound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfTrappingReturnCarry.overlappingMidpointReturns_twoPow_le_realBound"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/n